msgid "Factory Pattern for Dynamic Scripts"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For scenarios where you need to load scripts dynamically at runtime, use the "
"factory pattern:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This approach is perfect for applications that need to execute user-provided "
"scripts or\n"
"load scripts from external sources.  Note that the execution of the script "
"is fully sandboxed.\n"
"Only the methods exposed by the Context can be invoked from within the "
"script."
msgstr ""

msgid "Error Handling and Debugging"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"JavaScript errors are propagated as Java exceptions, making debugging "
"straightforward:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Build-time Magic"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Behind the scenes, the extension performs build-time code generation, "
"creating:"
msgstr ""

msgid "**CDI Bean Classes**: `{InterfaceName}_CDI` - Injectable CDI beans"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Factory Classes**: `{InterfaceName}_Factory` - Injectable factory beans"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Proxy Classes**: `{InterfaceName}_Proxy` - Generated by quickjs4j"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Context Builtins**: `{ContextName}_Builtins` - JavaScript-accessible Java "
"methods"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This build-time approach ensures minimal runtime overhead while providing "
"full IDE\n"
"support with code completion and type checking."
msgstr ""

msgid "Performance Considerations"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The QuickJS engine is designed for lightweight, fast JavaScript execution. "
"Combined with\n"
"Quarkus's build-time optimizations, the extension provides:"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Fast Startup**: Minimal impact on application startup time"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Low Memory Footprint**: Efficient memory usage for JavaScript execution"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Native Image Support**: Full compatibility with GraalVM native images"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Build-time Validation**: Early detection of interface mismatches and "
"errors"
msgstr ""

msgid "Use Cases"
msgstr ""

msgid "The Quarkus quickjs4j extension is perfect for:"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Business Rules Engines**: Implement configurable business logic"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Template Processing**: Generate dynamic content with JavaScript templates"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Algorithm Integration**: Leverage existing JavaScript algorithms and "
"libraries"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**User Scripting**: Allow power users to customize application behavior"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Configuration Logic**: Implement complex configuration scenarios"
msgstr ""

msgid "Current Status and Future Plans"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The extension is currently in **experimental status**, meaning APIs may "
"evolve based on\n"
"community feedback. We're actively working on:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Enhanced error reporting and debugging capabilities"
msgstr ""

msgid "Performance optimizations"
msgstr ""

msgid "Configurable JavaScript engine options"
msgstr ""

msgid "Improved IDE integration and tooling"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In particular, we have a lot of work to do in optimizing performance.  There "
"are\n"
"clear tradeoffs to consider around flexibility and speed, as well as "
"customization.\n"
"The current experimental implementation takes a very conservative approach "
"to\n"
"ensure full sandboxing and thread safety.  The result is a slower "
"implementation,\n"
"but one that is guaranteed to be thread safe and fully sandboxed."
msgstr ""

msgid "Getting Involved"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Quarkus quickjs4j extension is part of the Quarkiverse ecosystem and "
"welcomes community\n"
"contributions. Whether you're interested in:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Reporting bugs or requesting features"
msgstr ""

msgid "Contributing code improvements"
msgstr ""

